&Q000562 = Letter from Sîn-illat to Iddin-Dagan about confronting the Martu
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.3.2.01
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.3.2.01&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

1. lugal-ŋa₂ u₃-na-dug₄
#lem: lugal[king]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: Speak to my lord: this is what @wPN{@wDN{Sîn}-illat} the general, your servant, says: 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. {m}{d}suen-illat ra-bi-si₂-ka₃-tum-ma
#lem: Sinillat[1]PN; rabizigatum[military official]
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. arad-zu na-ab-be₂-a
#lem: arad[slave]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. ka-ku-la-tum{ki#} gaba-ri gid₂-da-ŋu₁₀-ne
#lem: Kakkulatum[1]SN; gabari[equal]; gid[long]
#tr.en: When I moved opposite @wSN{Kakkulātum}, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

5. mar-tu {ŋiš}tukul#-ta šubtum₆-ta im-zig₃
#lem: Martu[1 Amorite]; tukul[weapon]; šubtum[dwelling]; zig[rise]
#tr.en: the @wEN{Martu} rose up from their ambush with their weapons (?). 
#etcsl: line-id=5

6. ŋe₂₆-e X [...]-ga-ŋu₁₀-ne [...] X 70 i₃-dab₅
#lem: ŋaʾe[I]; X; X; X; X; n; dab[seize]
#tr.en: When I ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=6

7. ka-ku-la-tum{ki#}-še₃ ba-ni-in-kur₉
#lem: Kakkulatum[1]SN; kur[enter]
#tr.en: I captured 70 (?) …… and brought them into @wSN{Kakkulātum}. 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. tukum-bi lugal-ŋu₁₀ ugnim-ma tuš-u₃-bi ab-be₂
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]; ugnim[army]; tuš[sit (down)]; e[speak]
#tr.en: If my lord arranges for the troops to encamp, 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. {kuš}a-ŋa₂-la₂ keše₂-da-bi šu he₂-mi-ib-da₁₃-da₁₃
#lem: aŋala[leather sack]; kešed[bind]; šu[hand]; taka[set aside]
#tr.en: let him have them take their tied-up leather sacks. 
#etcsl: line-id=9

10. tukum-bi lugal-ŋu₁₀ ugnim-ma nu-tuš-u₃-bi ab-be₂
#lem: tukumbi[if]; lugal[king]; ugnim[army]; tuš[sit (down)]; e[speak]
#tr.en: If my lord arranges for the troops not to encamp, 
#etcsl: line-id=10

11. (1:he₂-em-ma-sug₂-ge-eš:1) (2:lugal-ŋu₁₀ he₂-en-zu:2)
#lem: gub[stand]; lugal[king]; zu[know]
#tr.en: @varh[t3201.v1]{then let them stay put } @vart[t3201.v2,t3201.v1]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} then let them go }. @varh[t3201.v3]{May my lord know } @vart[t3201.v4,t3201.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} This is urgent }! 
#etcsl: line-id=11

:11v.1.1: ($2 mss. have instead:$) he₂-em-ma-sub₂-be₂-eš
#lem: ŋen[go]
:11v.2.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) a-ma-[ru]-kam
#lem: amaru[flood]







